DESCRIPTION:GHOSTWOMAN itself only exists because Uschenko and van Dessel w
 ere the ones “stupid enough to commit to it”. Conceived by Uschenko af
 ter cutting his teeth as a touring multi-instrumentalist\, the project was
  brought to life in an abandoned farmhouse in Diamond City\, Alberta. Ther
 e\, for two months\, he would make the self-released\, self-titled debut a
 lbum which was produced and dubbed directly to custom-made cassette tapes.
  The music has always been beautifully inhospitable\, earned only by those
  curious enough to seek it out. — Dine Alone Records Presented by Get To
